{
  /* The node side: pipeline stages, the API, and the config files that run in
     the same process. Module resolution is nodenext because that is literally
     how these files run — tsx and node ESM — so a missing `.js` on a relative
     import is an error here rather than a crash the first time you run the
     stage. The client (src/web) is bundled by vite and uses Bundler
     resolution instead; see src/web/tsconfig.json. */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "nodenext",
    "moduleResolution": "nodenext",
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": [
    "src",
    "scripts",
    /* The production API. It runs the same way these do — node ESM, our own
       `.js`-suffixed relative imports — and it is the only copy of the server
       that users ever reach, so it is the last file that should go unchecked. */
    "api",
    /* evals/ runs the same way these do — tsx, node ESM — and reads the same
       artefacts, so it belongs to this project rather than to tests/. It is not
       part of the test suite: an eval calls a model and costs money. See
       evals/README.md. */
    "evals",
    "vite.config.ts",
    /* The API build. Same reasoning as vite.config.ts: it runs as node ESM in
       this project, so it is checked by this project. */
    "vite.api.config.ts",
    /* Which now also pulls in tests/store-migration-registry.ts, because the
       three vitest projects derive their file lists from `TEST_LANES` rather
       than restating them — one manifest, one verdict per file. The tests
       project checks that file too; a file in two projects is fine. */
    "vitest.config.ts",
    /* `vitest.spike.config.ts` was here, and was deleted with stage T-D on
       2026-09-04 along with tests/setup/spike-db.ts: the private-postgres
       project and tests/setup/private-db*.ts are what replaced them. */
    /* Stage A's witness 2 in
       docs/plans/260903f-delete-the-spideryarn-store-flag-and-the-filesystem-store.md:
       the instrumented run that produced tests/store-migration-witness.json.
       **Kept rather than thrown away, because that JSON is a measurement with a
       date on it and the tree keeps moving** — it recorded 588 test files and the
       import walk saw 597 ninety minutes later. Whoever needs to re-take it needs
       this. It is not wired into vitest.config.ts and `npm test` never loads it;
       run it deliberately:

         FSW_OUT=<path>.jsonl npx vitest run --config ./vitest.witness.config.ts

       Deleted with the filesystem store in stage G, when there is nothing left to
       instrument. */
    "vitest.witness.config.ts",
    "drizzle.config.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["src/web"]
}
